{"name":"Freesia Purple","hex":"#b3b0d4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"freesia","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any flowering plant of the genus Freesia, native to South Africa."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/freesia"},{"term":"purple","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour between red and blue; violet, though often closer to magenta.","Any non-spectral colour on the line of purples on a colour chromaticity diagram or a colour wheel between violet and red."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a purple hue.","Not predominantly red or blue, but having a mixture of Democrat and Republican support."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/purple"}],"entries":[{"title":"Freesia","blocks":[{"text":"Freesia is a genus of herbaceous perennial flowering plants in the family Iridaceae, first described as a genus in 1866 by Christian Friedrich Ecklon (1886) and named after the German botanist and medical practitioner, Friedrich Freese (1795–1876). It is native to the eastern side of southern Africa, from Kenya south to South Africa, most species being found in Cape Provinces. Species of the former genus Anomatheca are now included in Freesia. The plants commonly known as \"freesias\", with fragrant funnel-shaped flowers, are cultivated hybrids of a number of Freesia species. Some other species are also grown as ornamental plants."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Freesia.jpg/330px-Freesia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Freesia"},{"title":"Purple","blocks":[{"text":"Purple is a color similar in appearance to violet light. In the RYB color model historically used in the arts, purple is a secondary color created by combining red and blue pigments. In the CMYK color model used in modern printing, purple is made by combining magenta pigment with cyan pigment, black pigment, or both. In the RGB color model used in computer and television screens, purple is created by mixing red and blue light in order to create colors that appear similar to violet light. According to color theory, purple is considered a cool color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg/330px-Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purple"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Freesia_refracta_%28Jacq.%29_Klatt_%28AM_AK333551-2%29.jpg/120px-Freesia_refracta_%28Jacq.%29_Klatt_%28AM_AK333551-2%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Freesia_refracta_%28Jacq.%29_Klatt_%28AM_AK333551-2%29.jpg/250px-Freesia_refracta_%28Jacq.%29_Klatt_%28AM_AK333551-2%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Freesia_refracta_%28Jacq.%29_Klatt_%28AM_AK333551-2%29.jpg/120px-Freesia_refracta_%28Jacq.%29_Klatt_%28AM_AK333551-2%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFreesia_refracta_(Jacq.)_Klatt_(AM_AK333551-2).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Flower_March_2010-2.jpg/120px-Flower_March_2010-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Flower_March_2010-2.jpg/250px-Flower_March_2010-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Flower_March_2010-2.jpg/120px-Flower_March_2010-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&u